Package: next-partitioner
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k
Installer-Menu-Item: 4200
Maintainer: next68k-linux <https://github.com/dannydorazio/next68k-linux>
Depends: cdebconf-udeb, di-utils, e2fsprogs-udeb
Provides: created-fstab, made-filesystems, mounted-partitions, partitioned-harddrives
Section: debian-installer
Priority: standard
Description: Partition a disk with a NeXT disk label
 Gives a disk a NeXT disk label with the root file system, swap and the
 boot partition the NeXT Linux loader reads the kernel from, makes the
 file systems and mounts them on /target.  Takes the place of partman,
 since parted has no NeXT labels.
